model {
  extend basalt.frameworkRelease {
    metadata {
      constraint "Every host build embeds all canonical framework identities plus its checked producer before bundling, and an exported qualification snapshot when one is supplied. Canonical identities come from source-bound rebuilds, so reproducible bytes stay admitted across releases; changed framework bytes need a new canonical entry. Approved pre-enrollment releases are canonical qualifications bound to pinned rebuild evidence and never claim a serving-byte match. A freshly prepared host admits canonical framework bytes without producer enrollment; each newly committed identity must match the exact server, browser and runtime bytes from its reviewed Linux source build. Canonical build inputs remain separate from the generated runtime registry so Worker bundles embed history once. Compact generated storage decodes to the identical ordered publication tuples and hashes before admission. Offline source verification reproduces preparation replacement semantics and accepts generated registry data only against the checked candidate, producer, canonical identities and both publication hashes. App builds cannot enroll identities, and runtime admission remains offline and exact."
    }
  }
}
